' 3. Forgot / reset password
' Use case: Forgot password · Actor: Guest (an Admin can send the same link from Users & roles)
'
' Design patterns:
'   - Strategy + Factory + Dependency injection: «interface» Mailer chosen by mailerFromConfig(), injected into
'     createAccountSecurityService (services/mail/mailer.ts, services/account-security.service.ts)
'   - Unit of work: new password saved, link used and every session ended in one transaction
'   - Chain of responsibility: rateLimit middleware on both requests
'   - Repository
' Lifelines use BCE stereotypes: «boundary» screens and outside services, «control» use-case logic (controllers,
' services, and the adapter interfaces in front of outside services), «entity» stored data (repository, stores);
' the database keeps its own symbol.
@startuml 03 Reset password
title 3. Forgot / reset password
autonumber
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor Guest
boundary "Web app" as Web
control "Auth controller" as Ctrl
control "Account security\nservice" as Sec
control "«interface»\nMailer" as Mailer
entity "Repository" as Repo
database "Database" as DB
boundary "Email service" as Email

note over Web, Ctrl : «Chain of responsibility»: rateLimit before each controller

Guest -> Web : enter email
Web -> Ctrl : POST /api/auth/password/forgot
Ctrl -> Sec : requestReset(email)
Sec -> Repo : find active account by email
Repo -> DB : SELECT
opt active account, under the hourly limit
  Sec -> Repo : create reset token (hash stored)
  Repo -> DB : INSERT account_tokens
  Sec -> Mailer : send(reset link)
  note right of Mailer : «Strategy»\nSMTP / console / memory
  Mailer -> Email : SMTP
end
Ctrl --> Web : always the same answer
Web --> Guest : "If an account uses that address, a link is on its way"

== Later: the email link ==
Guest -> Web : open link, enter new password
Web -> Ctrl : POST /api/auth/password/reset (token, password)
Ctrl -> Sec : resetPassword()
group «Unit of work» withTransaction()
  Sec -> Repo : token valid, unused, not expired? → mark used
  Sec -> Repo : save new password hash
  Sec -> Repo : token version + 1 (every session ends)
  Sec -> Repo : mark email confirmed
  Repo -> DB : UPDATE …
end
alt link invalid or expired
  Sec --> Web : 400 "This link has expired"
end
Ctrl --> Web : done
Web --> Guest : go to sign in
@enduml
